course: dictionary
lesson: 7043
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the clues in the sentence show you which one the writer means. «In the cold, dark, narrow passage he lags behind.» Cold, dark and narrow are the clues: a passage here is a narrow way that you go along.
explain: «Read the passage carefully, then answer the questions.» In school, a passage is a short part of a text. The words read and answer tell you that. Ask yourself: what meaning would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The passage of time has made you taller.» Here the passage of time means time going by. «The ships made the passage across the ocean» means a journey, especially by ship. Same word, different meaning, so always check the context first.
fact: A passage is a narrow way, such as a corridor or path, that you go along.
fact: A passage is also a short part of a book, speech or piece of music, as in «read the passage».
fact: A passage can mean a journey, especially by ship, as in «the passage across the ocean».
fact: «The passage of time» means time going by.
fact: In a formal sense, the passage of a law means the law being accepted.
exercise: «In the cold, dark, narrow passage he lags behind.» In this sentence, what is a passage? | A piece of music | A short part of a book | A journey by ship | *A narrow way that you go along
exercise: In English lessons, what does «read the passage» mean? | A narrow corridor in a school | A ship's journey across the sea | Time going by | *A short part of a text
exercise: What does «the passage of time» mean? | *Time going by | A short piece of a book | A journey on a ship | A narrow path through the woods
test: «Badger's great secret: there is an underground passage from the river-bank into Toad Hall.» What kind of passage is this? | A journey by ship | A short part of a book | The passage of a law | *A narrow way that you go along
test: «The ship's passage across the ocean took three months.» What does passage mean? | A narrow way under the ground | A short part of a book | *A journey, especially by ship | Time going by
exam: «He found a stormy passage at the tip of South America.» What does passage mean here? | A narrow corridor | The passage of time | *A journey by sea | A short part of a book
